WEBVTT

00:14.521 --> 00:17.899
[playing classical tune]

00:32.622 --> 00:33.790
[song ends]

00:33.874 --> 00:35.375
[audience applauds]

00:37.169 --> 00:39.129
[Sumi] <i>Sixty percent bloom today, huh?</i>

00:40.589 --> 00:42.591
[opening theme song playing]

00:53.769 --> 00:58.106
FOOL NIGHT

02:11.221 --> 02:12.556
[Yomiko] New shoes, huh?

02:12.639 --> 02:14.474
Someone has expensive taste.

02:15.517 --> 02:17.102
Yeah, so when's the first payday?

02:18.061 --> 02:20.939
Here. An employee handbook and staff ID.

02:21.731 --> 02:22.816
It'll be a temp job.

02:22.899 --> 02:25.110
You're working in
the Spiriflor Locator Division.

02:26.403 --> 02:28.989
Your job is to work through
the Missing Spiriflor Reports

02:29.072 --> 02:31.074
that come to Transflora Medical,
all right?

02:31.533 --> 02:33.785
While we look for them,
the requests keep piling up,

02:33.869 --> 02:36.037
so the whole system's breaking down.

02:36.121 --> 02:38.748
I would take any job
for that amount of money.

02:39.291 --> 02:41.543
All right, well I'm going to reception.

02:41.626 --> 02:43.545
You work in reception here, too?

02:43.628 --> 02:45.755
I work a bunch of jobs here.

02:45.839 --> 02:47.507
That's why I'm in the Unsection.

02:47.591 --> 02:48.967
[cell phone ringing]

02:50.051 --> 02:50.886
Yeah?

02:50.969 --> 02:53.972
Oh, sure. I'll be right there.

02:55.599 --> 02:57.183
We have a client already.

03:06.443 --> 03:08.528
- [siren wails]
- [medic] Heart rate rapidly increasing.

03:08.612 --> 03:11.948
I'm not able to get the bleeding to stop.
The wound is too deep.

03:12.574 --> 03:15.118
This man will die
before we reach the hospital.

03:15.869 --> 03:17.370
You won't allow him to die.

03:17.454 --> 03:18.747
[medics gasp]

03:18.830 --> 03:22.375
If no one's able to save him,
get him to Transflora Medical.

03:23.209 --> 03:24.544
[medic] But, detective…

03:32.344 --> 03:33.261
INTAKE FORM
SUMI MATSUNO

03:33.345 --> 03:36.556
[Yomiko] What? Sumi Matsuno? That's you?

03:36.640 --> 03:37.515
Who?

03:37.599 --> 03:39.392
You've seen her poster around,
haven't you?

03:39.476 --> 03:41.394
Come on, she's the pianist Sumi Matsuno.

03:41.478 --> 03:42.604
She's amazing!

03:42.687 --> 03:44.439
I'm hardly a pianist.

03:44.522 --> 03:47.567
I have a lot more to learn.
I haven't even finished school.

03:47.651 --> 03:50.862
Hmm. You must be in
one of those fancy music-- [grunts]

03:50.946 --> 03:53.406
I'm sorry about him.
He's new to this work.

03:53.490 --> 03:54.908
So what's the reason for your visit?

03:55.951 --> 03:58.703
I was hoping you could
find my father's Spiriflor.

04:00.288 --> 04:02.958
My family wasn't wealthy by any means.

04:03.541 --> 04:05.293
My father underwent Transfloration

04:05.377 --> 04:07.712
and put me through university
with the subsidy.

04:07.796 --> 04:11.341
But I never saw him again
after he had the procedure.

04:12.133 --> 04:14.302
I am who I am today thanks to my father.

04:14.386 --> 04:16.680
I just want to be able
to mourn him properly.

04:18.723 --> 04:20.141
I'll need some information.

04:20.225 --> 04:22.060
What is his name and approximate age?

04:22.143 --> 04:23.019
TRANSFLORATION APPLICATION

04:23.103 --> 04:24.145
"Shogo Matsuno.

04:24.229 --> 04:27.315
Piano instructor at
the Second National University of Music."

04:27.399 --> 04:31.611
According to his records,
the reason for his Transfloration was…

04:31.695 --> 04:33.071
MERCURY POISONING

04:35.115 --> 04:36.574
It was suicide, right?

04:38.451 --> 04:39.577
Like you said, Sumi,

04:39.661 --> 04:42.706
he likely underwent Transfloration
for the subsidy money.

04:43.790 --> 04:45.792
If a Transfloration applicant is dying,

04:45.875 --> 04:47.711
we aren't allowed to turn them away.

04:48.420 --> 04:50.630
It's not uncommon for people
who undergo the procedure

04:50.714 --> 04:52.465
to leave their families, though.

04:52.549 --> 04:54.050
They search for a place to die

04:54.134 --> 04:57.262
and many end up going
to their workplace to do it.

04:57.345 --> 05:00.515
The Seed that was planted in Shogo
was a Sawafutagi Seed.

05:01.516 --> 05:03.476
It's been three years since his procedure.

05:03.560 --> 05:05.603
He's a full-fledged Spiriflor by now.

05:05.687 --> 05:08.523
To start, I want to search
the university campus.

05:08.606 --> 05:10.942
[Sumi] Are Sawafutagi plants
common or rare?

05:11.026 --> 05:12.110
Common.

05:12.193 --> 05:15.655
Then, if he's one of those plants,
how will you know which one he is?

05:15.739 --> 05:18.116
[Yomiko] Normally it would be difficult,
but lucky for us,

05:19.159 --> 05:21.745
this man can communicate
directly with Spiriflora.

05:23.538 --> 05:24.539
Huh?

05:27.167 --> 05:28.710
We have to go back now.

05:29.419 --> 05:31.504
I'll reach out if we find something.

05:32.547 --> 05:33.715
All right.

05:33.798 --> 05:35.050
[cell phone ringing]

05:35.133 --> 05:37.052
Sorry, but I really have to take this.

05:38.887 --> 05:41.598
Hello? Okay. Really?

05:43.767 --> 05:45.935
Shouldn't you be going back with her?

05:46.561 --> 05:48.229
You're really suspicious of me.

05:48.313 --> 05:49.814
Obviously I am!

05:49.898 --> 05:51.441
I'm desperately searching for him

05:51.524 --> 05:53.818
and you just happen
to speak with Spiriflora?

05:54.486 --> 05:57.072
You say you're desperate,
but it's been three years.

05:57.822 --> 05:59.449
[stutters] Well, that's because…

05:59.908 --> 06:02.368
It's because
you've always hated your father.

06:02.911 --> 06:03.995
[gasps]

06:04.704 --> 06:07.082
When you were talking about him
in the reception room,

06:07.791 --> 06:10.835
the Spiriflora nearby sensed your hatred.

06:11.878 --> 06:13.630
There's a reason for that, right?

06:13.713 --> 06:16.841
What do you actually want to do
if you find your father's Spiriflor?

06:18.009 --> 06:20.261
If you want to get rid of it,
I'll help you.

06:20.345 --> 06:21.346
For a price.

06:23.890 --> 06:25.350
I want to burn it.

06:27.685 --> 06:30.980
I want to burn my dad's Spiriflor.

06:32.607 --> 06:33.733
[lighter clicks]

06:44.160 --> 06:45.245
[exhales]

06:46.955 --> 06:48.248
[Yomiko] Wait a minute, detective.

06:48.331 --> 06:50.625
You can't just have me
turn him into a Spiriflor.

06:50.708 --> 06:51.709
I need his permission first.

06:51.793 --> 06:53.711
He's on the verge of death as we speak.

06:53.795 --> 06:55.296
You know the recent
Transfloration murders?

06:55.380 --> 06:57.340
This man's the sole survivor of one.

06:57.423 --> 06:59.008
- Uh--
- You can save a person

06:59.092 --> 07:01.553
on the verge of death by planting
a Seed in them, right?

07:01.636 --> 07:03.721
He may know who the serial killer is.

07:03.805 --> 07:05.140
So this is all for your investiga--

07:05.223 --> 07:07.642
- Twenty people have been murdered already.
- [gasps]

07:07.725 --> 07:10.979
We have to do everything we can
to prevent any more murders.

07:11.062 --> 07:13.898
We don't have time to worry about
someone's will or what the rules are.

07:13.982 --> 07:15.650
Do the Transfloration.

07:15.733 --> 07:17.152
You have to keep him alive.

07:20.196 --> 07:22.949
Inose. Get permission
for a Transfloration.

07:23.032 --> 07:24.200
[Inose] Uh, on it!

07:37.464 --> 07:39.340
[playing silently]

07:42.469 --> 07:44.512
So you love playing the piano, right?

07:44.596 --> 07:45.930
- [Sumi] Not at all.
- Huh?

07:46.973 --> 07:48.057
[Sumi] I hate it.

07:48.141 --> 07:49.934
I was forced to play.

07:50.018 --> 07:51.352
[thunderclap]

07:51.436 --> 07:52.353
[inaudible]

07:54.856 --> 07:57.025
My father was merciless
when it came to the piano.

07:57.609 --> 08:00.612
The slightest mistake would enrage him
and he'd beat me.

08:00.695 --> 08:03.323
He'd keep doing that
until I played it perfectly.

08:03.948 --> 08:06.201
Is that why you want
to burn his Spiraflor?

08:06.284 --> 08:07.327
[Sumi] Yes.

08:07.869 --> 08:09.954
Even though he's dead,
I'm still haunted by him

08:10.038 --> 08:11.581
whenever I play the piano.

08:12.290 --> 08:13.291
[Toshiro] Hmm.

08:13.374 --> 08:14.918
[Sumi] What's something that you love?

08:16.586 --> 08:17.795
[Toshiro] Mm.

08:17.879 --> 08:18.880
Um, money?

08:20.882 --> 08:22.800
Yeah, well, money is pretty important.

08:23.468 --> 08:24.719
[Toshiro sighs]

08:26.304 --> 08:27.931
[distorted static]

08:29.265 --> 08:30.934
[detective] Why'd he end up like this?

08:31.601 --> 08:33.436
When the host is on the verge of death,

08:33.520 --> 08:34.521
the Seed that was planted

08:34.604 --> 08:37.106
can sometimes experience
an explosive growth.

08:37.190 --> 08:39.192
It happens to avoid death.

08:39.275 --> 08:41.986
All right, but was there nothing you
could've done to save his mouth?

08:42.070 --> 08:43.863
I needed him able to speak.

08:43.947 --> 08:45.323
I did what you asked of me.

08:45.406 --> 08:46.407
[door closes]

08:46.491 --> 08:48.868
Pardon me. His parents are here.

08:48.952 --> 08:50.370
[gasps]

08:53.373 --> 08:54.582
[woman gasping]

08:59.087 --> 09:00.922
[sobbing]

09:10.557 --> 09:12.475
CAMPUS MAP
TO UNIVERSITY SPIRIFLORA FOREST

09:13.184 --> 09:15.019
[thunder rolling]

09:30.743 --> 09:34.539
I didn't know there was a forest
behind the university, to be honest.

09:34.622 --> 09:36.499
It seems pretty big.

09:36.583 --> 09:37.584
It's massive.

09:37.667 --> 09:40.420
It covers the space of a small mountain,
if I remember right.

09:40.503 --> 09:41.921
Yeah, that's huge.

09:42.505 --> 09:44.674
Damn, there's no way we'll find it.

09:50.805 --> 09:51.806
This way.

09:54.684 --> 09:55.768
Oh, here it is.

09:56.853 --> 09:58.646
Mm-hmm, this is right.

09:58.730 --> 10:00.523
- Before anybody comes here--
- Stop lying.

10:00.607 --> 10:01.858
[gasps]

10:01.941 --> 10:03.568
Hey, wait a second.

10:03.651 --> 10:06.904
That Spiriflor back there
is clearly not a Sawafutagi.

10:06.988 --> 10:09.782
It's completely different from the photo
your coworker showed us.

10:09.907 --> 10:10.950
[Toshiro panting]

10:11.034 --> 10:14.871
Wait. [panting] Wait. I… I'm sorry.

10:18.207 --> 10:19.626
This time I'll do it right.

10:20.585 --> 10:23.338
Okay and what exactly do you mean by that?

10:24.130 --> 10:25.173
Don't you get it?

10:25.256 --> 10:27.717
I want to burn my father's Spiriflor
to the ground.

10:29.260 --> 10:30.219
You're scared, right?

10:31.804 --> 10:34.015
If you hate playing the piano,

10:34.098 --> 10:36.309
why not just quit and never play again?

10:37.810 --> 10:40.313
Trust me, I would've
done that already if I could.

10:40.772 --> 10:43.441
But try putting yourself in my shoes
for a second.

10:44.651 --> 10:46.527
My father gave up his life in exchange

10:46.611 --> 10:48.821
for the money I needed to pay
for university.

10:49.530 --> 10:51.199
And because he did that for me…

10:51.282 --> 10:54.118
I… I had to become the best pianist.

10:55.536 --> 10:59.582
Aside from that, how is a woman supposed
to survive by herself in this world?

10:59.666 --> 11:01.167
Am I supposed to find a job?

11:01.250 --> 11:02.794
Where? In the sex industry?

11:02.877 --> 11:04.379
In a factory? Waiting tables?

11:04.462 --> 11:07.423
All those people are forgotten
and left to die in the streets.

11:07.507 --> 11:09.967
The only thing I have is the piano.

11:10.051 --> 11:11.344
It's all I've ever done.

11:11.427 --> 11:13.012
It's all I was allowed to do.

11:15.223 --> 11:16.391
That's why I want…

11:17.100 --> 11:19.811
I want to be able to forget my father
once and for all.

11:19.894 --> 11:22.814
I despise the piano
because I was forced to play it.

11:22.897 --> 11:24.649
I want to learn to love it again.

11:24.732 --> 11:26.192
[wind gushes]

11:27.026 --> 11:28.569
[somber instrumental music playing]

11:33.699 --> 11:36.285
I don't have the ability
to locate or talk to Spiriflora.

11:38.037 --> 11:41.707
All I can do
is hear the Spiraflora's voices

11:41.791 --> 11:45.503
and identify them
only after they've been found.

11:46.045 --> 11:47.880
I'm disappointed to hear that.

11:48.673 --> 11:51.384
We need professional help with this.

11:59.016 --> 12:00.059
Excuse me.

12:00.726 --> 12:02.103
Stay away from us, okay?

12:02.186 --> 12:03.396
His face…

12:03.938 --> 12:05.189
[sniffling]

12:05.273 --> 12:07.066
He's…

12:07.150 --> 12:09.819
[sobbing] I just wanted to hold his hand.

12:09.902 --> 12:11.904
- [cell phone buzzing]
- [couple sobbing]

12:11.988 --> 12:13.948
[somber instrumental music continues]

12:20.288 --> 12:23.082
Okay. Got it. Thanks, Yomiko.

12:23.875 --> 12:27.378
Since he was a pianist, he likely would
have undergone Complete Transfloration

12:27.462 --> 12:28.796
somewhere near a piano.

12:29.297 --> 12:33.509
She also said, from far away,
Sawafutagi kind of look like fireworks.

12:33.593 --> 12:37.054
- Huh?
- Mm. Or was it sparklers?

12:37.138 --> 12:38.890
[piano music plays softly]

12:38.973 --> 12:41.976
Sounds like someone's
playing the piano. Let's go.

12:53.696 --> 12:55.114
[piano music continues]

12:56.491 --> 12:59.452
They're impressed because you're young,
Sumi, not because of skill.

12:59.535 --> 13:02.455
You really need to keep practicing
if you want to be good.

13:03.247 --> 13:04.957
[sighs] You're sure
you're Matsuno's daughter?

13:06.292 --> 13:07.543
How boring.

13:15.092 --> 13:16.344
I hear one.

13:16.427 --> 13:19.138
"This pianist is absolutely terrible…

13:19.222 --> 13:21.891
How did somebody like them get…

13:21.974 --> 13:23.851
get accepted…

13:23.935 --> 13:25.394
They're really awful."

13:28.689 --> 13:29.732
That's it.

13:34.820 --> 13:36.280
[Sumi] Sawafutagi.

13:40.785 --> 13:44.288
It's reaching toward the school.

13:46.499 --> 13:47.750
It's my father.

13:48.834 --> 13:51.879
He keeps on complaining about
whoever's playing the piano.

13:53.631 --> 13:55.341
He's the same as always.

14:00.930 --> 14:01.806
[lighter licking]

14:03.432 --> 14:04.809
[distorted static]

14:09.188 --> 14:10.815
[Toshiro] You're conflicted.

14:10.898 --> 14:12.191
[Sumi] No, I'm not.

14:12.275 --> 14:15.027
Your father's Spiriflor
feels it within you.

14:15.111 --> 14:16.445
You can't hide from it.

14:16.529 --> 14:19.949
Maybe you shouldn't be doing this
if you're going to regret it.

14:20.032 --> 14:21.075
It's not that.

14:21.867 --> 14:25.079
I'm thankful he raised me…
[sniffles] which makes this difficult.

14:36.966 --> 14:38.217
[gasps]

14:41.429 --> 14:44.891
Starting tomorrow,
you have to practice hard on the piano.

14:44.974 --> 14:46.309
[young Sumi] Mm-hmm.

14:49.854 --> 14:52.732
[Sumi] Either be a good father,
or a bad one.

14:52.815 --> 14:54.025
Make up your mind.

14:55.651 --> 14:59.113
But there's just no way I'll forgive you
for all of the violence.

15:00.197 --> 15:02.241
I never deserved what you did to me.

15:02.325 --> 15:04.160
[gentle music]

15:07.955 --> 15:09.373
Translate what I said.

15:09.457 --> 15:11.375
Well, all I can do is hear--

15:11.459 --> 15:12.960
Tell him what I said.

15:13.044 --> 15:15.880
I don't want this to end
without him knowing how I feel.

15:17.048 --> 15:18.215
[hesitates] But…

15:19.008 --> 15:20.217
[groans softly]

15:20.301 --> 15:22.345
[grunts] Look, it won't work.

15:22.970 --> 15:24.096
It will.

15:24.180 --> 15:25.389
[Toshiro gasps]

15:29.477 --> 15:31.020
- But why?
- [lighter clicking]

15:31.729 --> 15:32.563
Why?

15:32.647 --> 15:34.482
- [lighter clinking]
- [Sumi sobs]

15:36.359 --> 15:37.860
[melancholy music playing]

15:42.448 --> 15:43.532
[gasps]

15:45.868 --> 15:47.286
[gasping]

15:51.499 --> 15:52.500
[grunts softly]

15:53.334 --> 15:54.794
What… is this?

15:59.548 --> 16:00.591
Say it.

16:01.842 --> 16:02.760
Tell him now!

16:02.843 --> 16:04.470
I'll never forgive him for what he did.

16:05.012 --> 16:05.846
You sure?

16:05.930 --> 16:07.348
- Please.
- Uh…

16:09.100 --> 16:10.434
[sighs in resignation]

16:11.394 --> 16:13.020
Your daughter won't…

16:13.104 --> 16:15.231
She won't forgive what you did to her.

16:15.314 --> 16:17.441
You made her play the piano
when she didn't want to,

16:17.525 --> 16:19.402
and you abused her.

16:19.485 --> 16:22.238
Because of what you did,
she hates the piano now.

16:30.121 --> 16:31.497
- [Shogo] Sumi?
- [gasps]

16:32.707 --> 16:33.708
[Toshiro] "Sumi."

16:33.791 --> 16:34.834
[Sumi gasps]

16:36.711 --> 16:38.713
[Toshiro as Shogo]
"The hatred I felt earlier…

16:39.380 --> 16:41.215
that was you, Sumi.

16:41.924 --> 16:44.635
Why do you hate me so much?

16:45.344 --> 16:46.762
And you hate the piano?

16:47.221 --> 16:48.431
Did you quit playing?"

16:49.015 --> 16:51.058
No, I… I still play all the time.

16:52.018 --> 16:54.478
Even though…
it's always been painful for me.

16:55.479 --> 16:56.981
[Toshiro] She didn't quit.

16:57.064 --> 16:59.400
Your strict teaching
really traumatized her.

16:59.942 --> 17:02.028
She said it's still painful.

17:03.654 --> 17:04.739
[gasps]

17:04.822 --> 17:06.323
[warbling]

17:06.907 --> 17:07.867
[as Shogo] "Painful?

17:08.701 --> 17:10.119
Of course it is.

17:10.202 --> 17:13.122
Everyone has to endure
unreasonable things in life."

17:14.415 --> 17:16.751
[voices overlapping] "You're very
fortunate to be where you are now.

17:16.834 --> 17:18.210
Try to remember that."

17:19.003 --> 17:20.963
[Shogo] I'm the one
who's keeping you alive,

17:21.047 --> 17:24.341
with your piano skills
and the Transfloration money.

17:28.596 --> 17:31.515
[Toshiro] How is she supposed
to respond to that?

17:31.599 --> 17:32.725
That's horrible!

17:32.808 --> 17:34.226
[melancholy music playing]

17:40.191 --> 17:41.859
<i>That's almost like saying,</i>

17:41.942 --> 17:45.321
"If I hadn't given birth to you,
you wouldn't even exist."

17:47.031 --> 17:48.991
You better apologize to her!

17:49.575 --> 17:53.079
Have you ever thought about the terror
she constantly endured because of you?

17:53.162 --> 17:54.205
[Sumi sobs]

17:59.502 --> 18:00.628
[Shogo] This is…

18:00.711 --> 18:02.755
Something's flowing to me from Sumi.

18:04.423 --> 18:05.925
So you're done playing?

18:06.425 --> 18:07.551
[young Sumi cries out]

18:09.053 --> 18:10.554
Playing's your only option.

18:10.638 --> 18:13.516
One day, you're going to be
grateful to your father.

18:13.599 --> 18:16.227
One day, you'll realize
that all this practice

18:16.310 --> 18:17.686
allowed you to have a good life.

18:18.771 --> 18:20.189
This is for your sake.

18:20.272 --> 18:21.607
<i>Are you listening?</i>

18:25.319 --> 18:27.488
- Get up.
- [young Sumi crying in pain]

18:28.489 --> 18:29.490
Now, go play.

18:30.032 --> 18:30.991
Leave her alone.

18:31.075 --> 18:32.535
[young Sumi sobbing]

18:33.494 --> 18:35.037
Stop it, please.

18:35.121 --> 18:36.789
[young Sumi continues sobbing]

18:36.872 --> 18:40.209
Starting tomorrow,
you have to practice hard on the piano.

18:40.292 --> 18:43.212
Mm-hmm. I will, don't worry.

18:43.295 --> 18:44.588
I love you, Dad.

18:47.299 --> 18:49.051
Don't you see what I'm doing for you?

18:49.135 --> 18:50.344
[young Sumi cries out]

18:51.679 --> 18:53.222
Why am I so oblivious?

18:54.723 --> 18:57.184
How could I ignore all this suffering?

18:58.686 --> 19:00.062
<i>I can see it.</i>

19:00.938 --> 19:02.106
I can hear it.

19:02.940 --> 19:04.525
Don't do this!

19:05.651 --> 19:06.652
Why?

19:10.030 --> 19:13.701
Why didn't I notice
while I was still human?

19:13.784 --> 19:15.202
[melancholy music continues]

19:20.666 --> 19:24.128
[voice trembling] I'm… sorry.

19:24.628 --> 19:26.589
[melancholy music continues]

19:33.095 --> 19:35.181
I'll never forgive what you've done.

19:36.599 --> 19:37.683
[sniffling]

19:44.565 --> 19:46.108
- [sniffling]
- [lighter clicks]

19:50.446 --> 19:51.572
But, Father…

19:53.574 --> 19:55.576
I'm going to make a piano out of you.

19:58.120 --> 19:59.371
[Toshiro groans]

20:01.248 --> 20:02.499
[body thumps]

20:04.793 --> 20:06.503
[classical piano music playing]

20:24.438 --> 20:25.940
[snapping]

20:37.284 --> 20:40.663
[Sumi] <i>From now on, you'll be right here.</i>

20:40.746 --> 20:42.665
<i>Right within my grasp.</i>

20:42.748 --> 20:43.958
[piano music continues]

20:46.585 --> 20:48.254
<i>This is what you get.</i>

20:48.879 --> 20:51.298
<i>It's my turn to make you do what I want.</i>

20:52.216 --> 20:53.926
[piano music continues]

20:57.137 --> 20:58.138
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

21:06.855 --> 21:08.023
[music ends]

21:09.108 --> 21:11.026
[audience applauding]

21:20.119 --> 21:21.537
[general indistinct chatter]

21:25.708 --> 21:28.168
[Toshiro]
<i>I think it's time I freed myself, too.</i>

21:32.339 --> 21:33.674
That was fun, right?

21:33.757 --> 21:35.509
[boy] Yeah, I wanna go again.

21:35.592 --> 21:37.636
Make sure you do your homework then.

21:37.720 --> 21:38.846
- [boy] What?
- [man laughs]

21:38.929 --> 21:40.222
[metal clanging]

21:40.306 --> 21:41.348
- [man] Uh…
- [woman] Uh?

21:44.768 --> 21:47.313
[Toshiro]
<i>I might actually get killed this time.</i>

21:48.188 --> 21:50.774
<i>But I have money now, and status.</i>

21:59.908 --> 22:02.202
[door unlocking]

22:03.579 --> 22:04.705
[door creaking]

22:15.591 --> 22:16.842
[voice trembling] Mom, are you…

22:18.093 --> 22:19.553
- [Kaori grunts]
- [Toshiro gasps]

22:19.636 --> 22:20.554
[Kaori panting]

22:20.637 --> 22:23.015
[both grunting, straining]

22:26.477 --> 22:28.062
[melancholy music playing]

22:29.313 --> 22:31.315
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

22:31.398 --> 22:33.484
[both continue grunting, straining]

22:35.027 --> 22:36.153
[grunting]

22:37.029 --> 22:38.322
[Toshiro] I'll kill you.

22:38.781 --> 22:39.990
Just die!

22:40.657 --> 22:42.701
Why won't you just die already?

22:42.785 --> 22:44.078
[Kaori straining]

22:44.161 --> 22:45.454
[woman sobbing]

22:48.290 --> 22:49.708
[grunting]

22:51.543 --> 22:53.212
[Kaori and Toshiro straining]

22:57.257 --> 22:58.759
[straining]

22:59.259 --> 23:01.178
[melancholy music continues]

23:08.769 --> 23:10.562
[straining, grunting stops]

23:16.693 --> 23:18.654
[gasping, coughing]

23:20.447 --> 23:22.032
[Kaori continues gasping]

23:32.167 --> 23:35.504
[man] Your son was involved
in a Transfloration related crime.

23:35.587 --> 23:38.924
The perpetrator's a person who gained
power through Transfloration.

23:39.007 --> 23:42.302
Turning humans into Spiriflor
has only brought tragedy.

23:42.386 --> 23:44.429
But, I'm sorry, who are you?

23:44.513 --> 23:45.722
I've come to recruit you.

23:46.431 --> 23:48.642
Transfloration should be stopped.

23:48.725 --> 23:50.727
And we are going to fight it.

23:52.229 --> 23:54.231
[closing theme song playing]
